commit e41e1c553b78fe123b07454bdc2513c307a29704
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Aug 11 16:23:58 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Aug 11 16:23:58 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): corroborate the lag verdict against the log, heal a rewound marker
    
    The offset marker lives inside the very sqlite file canonical_audit exists to
    judge, so deciding Check.lag from it alone made the innocence claim
    attacker-writable: rewind one integer in store_meta below an edited interior
    row and `sl store verify` downgraded tampering to a WARNING reading "not
    evidence of tampering". Lag now holds only when the log suffix past the offset
    is genuinely unindexed (_suffix_unindexed: line boundary, decodes, and the
    index has no row for it — a torn tail still counts, that IS the crash window).
    --deep gets the same corroboration, so "lag": true can no longer be stamped
    onto a tampered line in --json.
    
    And the remedy the gate advertises is a remedy again: tailing forward from a
    rewound offset re-executed INSERT for rows already present and raised a raw
    sqlite3.IntegrityError out of every read verb, making the state the gate calls
    recoverable a permanent dead end. catch_up answers the collision with the same
    rebuild it already runs when _prefix_intact fails one line earlier — the
    colliding rows are all reproducible from the canonical log, unlike the
    out-of-band rows _refuse_out_of_band protects. A duplicate id in the LOG (the
    one collision rebuild cannot resolve) now refuses by name instead of leaking
    the constraint error.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

