The corroboration fixes the narrow repro (a marker rewind directly over still-present rows is no longer called lag), but its “genuinely unindexed suffix” claim is stronger than its implementation: it checks only the first suffix row. In scratch testing, an index-only edit that rewinds the marker, removes that first row, updates the count marker, and poisons a later suffix row is labeled `lag_only=True` by the default gate. A log-only interior edit plus a valid appended row produces the same default benign label. `--deep` catches both, but its early break then reports `chain ok` over zero or only prefix ticks. I’m validating the user-visible remedy and exact CLI output next.
