Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Aug 11 15:58:06 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Aug 11 15:58:06 2026 -0500

    feat(loops): gate store verify/stats/ticks on canonical agreement
    
    `sl store verify` on a JSONL-canonical store now runs the agreement gate
    BEFORE the chain walk, and a divergence suppresses the chain verdict
    entirely rather than printing it beside a warning: the chain's verdict is
    worth nothing about an index the log does not support. rc=1, naming which
    check failed (offset / counts / last-line), in text and --json alike.
    
    Success labels say what was actually checked — "index chain intact; canonical
    parity checks pass (not deep)" for the quick path, "canonical content
    verified line-by-line; chain re-derived from the log" for --deep — plus a
    printed scope boundary: an unsealed fact edited in BOTH artifacts is out of
    scope, its witnesses being the fact signature and the next seal. Printed, not
    left in a docstring, so the output cannot quietly widen its claim.
    
    --deep streams the whole log (bounded memory; the 111MB live store audits in
    ~1.5s). stats/ticks run the same gate and refuse rather than serve derived
    data the log disowns.
    
    The gate resolves the artifacts purely (resolve_canonical_path +
    index_path_for) instead of through resolve_store_path: that path runs
    ensure_index, which repairs a stale index — and a repaired index agrees by
    construction, so a log-ahead-of-index store would have verified clean.
    Building an ABSENT index is still allowed there (fresh clone: no prior state
    to destroy, no divergence it can hide), keeping the store-verb existence
    contract intact. .db-canonical stores are untouched, pinned by a test.
    
    design/store/verify-canonical-agreement
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

