docs/scratch/080-overnight/store-dumps/fold-current.txt:52:design/horizon-build1-scope                                         high   1   6  2026-07-04  Horizon build-1 SCOPE (autonomous-run design entry): 'sl read <v> --lens horizon' lens-declared fetch. THE net-new piece: fetch_horizon reconstructs the OPEN (unsealed) window read-side — newest tick ts via existing tick query, Store.between(last_tick_ts, now), aggregate via the same payload-stats helper fetch_tick_windows uses — joined against each loop's declared Boundary (atoms/boundary.py). TickWindow models sealed ticks only; _vertex_period_start is runtime-only, so read-side reconstruction is the honest path. Render by boundary shape, no invented signals: count-based (after/every) -> numeric proximity 'n/N' (meter at TTY); kind-based (when) -> 'waiting on <kind> · N facts in window · last sealed <recency>' — NO fake progress bar (hlab is 100% kind-based, verified); vertex-level boundary -> one row. Loops with NO boundary are OMITTED (honest absence over invented glyph, per tier-one-home-inheritance); boundary-poor vertices like project degrade to near-one-line and that is correct. -q rollup 'vertex · N armed loops · N unsealed facts · last sealed <recency>'; -v adds window kind mix + boundary conditions; FULL adds last-tick detail. Piped = flat ledger, ISO stamps, width=None, register parity test. Deferred per 060-view-sequence: -v ETA extrapolation (needs inter-tick-interval stats); ⊘ lifecycle stays unwired (Horizon uses recency strings only — no smuggled staleness thresholds).
docs/scratch/080-overnight/store-dumps/fold-current.txt:87:design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity                        mid    1   4  2026-06-28  Nit-2 ruling (Kyle, 2026-06-28). store ticks/stats/verify share three distinguishable existence states, all at the shared chokepoint (before resolve_store_path, store.py:49): (1) absent .vertex -> ONE shared FileNotFoundError guard, clean 'vertex X does not exist' RC=1 across all three (not a ticks-only guard, which would trade one asymmetry for another). (2) present .vertex / absent .db -> RC=1 with a DISTINCT surfaced message ('store not yet materialized — no facts emitted'); ticks moves from its current RC=0-empty outlier to RC=1, matching stats/verify. Kyle: 'no store, no ticks, but it is an issue we should surface' — absent-db is never-materialized, a distinct state from written-and-empty (write-receipt-vs-temporal-query at the exit-code layer), so it earns its own message not a generic open-failure. (3) present .db / no matching ticks -> RC=0 empty, B1 scoped-message ('No ticks in the last Ns'). DEFERRED: lang.errors.ParseError escapes the cli/views/store.py:35 catch (neither ValueError nor FileNotFoundError) -> goes to thread:error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy, an exception-taxonomy fix broader than this build.
docs/scratch/080-overnight/store-dumps/fold-current.txt:132:implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped                         mid    1   3  2026-06-28  S7 shipped (7d23757): `store ticks [--chain]` + `store stats [--by-kind]`, lens-only over fetch_tick_windows (its first production consumer). --chain projects the per-tick attestation envelope (linkage/signature/cursor) and spans the FULL chain via all_names so it AGREES with store verify/stats (33==33==33); density default stays name-scoped (delta fields are same-series). fetch_tick_windows gained since=None + all_names (tests-only prior callers, default unchanged). Two-mode ticks avoids a dead --chain flag (honesty rule). zero golden regold.
docs/scratch/080-overnight/store-dumps/fold-current.txt:135:design/ls-as-stat-over-containment                                  mid    1   3  2026-06-30  sl ls reshaped as stat-over-containment: vertex⊃kind⊃fact = dir⊃subdir⊃file. ls lists entries one level down from where pointed, with uniform stat columns at every level (size=Σfacts, mtime=last-update, type=vertex-kind/fold-op). Composes by DESCENT not flags: 'sl ls'=vertices, 'sl ls project'=kinds, 'sl ls project --kind K'=facts(⇒read). ls owns structural levels (vertex/kind), read owns content level (fact). Designed divergence from unix: stats shown BY DEFAULT (not -l-gated) because vertices are few — the absent stat columns ARE the 'not terribly useful' complaint. mtime column = the resumption orient ('where did I leave off') at vertex granularity, answered before any lens runs. Re-bind not build: store stats --by-kind (S7) + store ticks + fetch_declarations already supply the data; net-new is one cheap max(ts) GROUP BY kind + a lens reshape. Design doc: docs/dev/ls-as-stat-over-containment-2026-06-29.md. Open decisions A-D + slice sketch S0-S4 in doc.
