docs/scratch/080-overnight/store-dumps/facts-60d.txt:199:mid       02:47 [observation] rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory: M3 ask: record every adapter loops hand-builds to reuse a painted renderer through run_cli. loops has TWO dispatch spines and both hand-build glue. SPINE 1 legacy run_cli path — commands/ still call painted.run_cli(fetch=, render=) directly; each supplies a render(ctx, data) closure that is pure adapter boilerplate translating painted's CliContext into a loops lens call. Inventory of the render closures: ls.py:204 (declarations_view) and :518 (kind_stat_view); population.py:81 (vertices_view); store.py:654 (tick_chain_view), :723 (stats_view), :788 (store_view); ticks.py:103 and stream.py:77 (resolve-then-call composition adapters); sync.py:170 and :321 (sync_view); devtools.py x4. The recurring glue is exactly: 'w = ctx.width if ctx.is_tty else None; return LENS(data, ctx.zoom, w, piped=not ctx.is_tty)'. Every one re-derives width-from-TTY and piped-from-TTY by hand. SPINE 2 new siftd-shape path — cli/dispatch.py:dispatch owns the same branches natively (action/interactive/live/static) and no longer routes static through run_cli; it computes width from sys.stdout.isatty() itself. DISSOLUTION: under a (data, fidelity, width) renderer contract where painted owns the fetch->render->emit loop and passes width already normalized (None=piped), every Spine-1 render closure collapses to nothing — the ctx.zoom/ctx.width/ctx.is_tty unpacking and the piped re-derivation are the whole adapter, and all of it is painted re-exposing what painted already knows. The closures exist only because loops re-reads TTY state painted computed one frame earlier.
docs/scratch/080-overnight/store-dumps/facts-60d.txt:203:mid       02:46 [observation] rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact: M3 exit criterion says loops semantic renderers must require no fabricated mode, TTY, or stream facts. loops VIOLATES this via one fact: piped. It is computed as (not ctx.is_tty) or (not sys.stdout.isatty()) and threaded as a keyword into ~11 lens entrypoints: declarations_view, kind_stat_view, vertices_view, store_view, tick_chain_view, stats_view, ticks_view, stream_view, confluence_view, horizon_view, graph_view, and the built-in fold_view. It is REDUNDANT: width already carries the same two-state contract (concrete int on a TTY, None when piped) — normalize_width and its docstring in lens_resolver.py state this explicitly, and every run_cli render closure sets width via 'w = ctx.width if ctx.is_tty else None' right beside 'piped=not ctx.is_tty'. So the same TTY bit is encoded TWICE at every call site, once as width=None and once as piped=True. Dissolution: lenses that branch on piped can branch on 'width is None' instead; piped as a param disappears and the fabricated-TTY-fact criterion is met with zero new painted machinery. This is deletable independently of the declaration grammar.
