commit b7d44c092a5366dad47100dee5a1603495ce1fc5
Author: Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 11 16:30:10 2026 -0500

    fix(tasks): readers resolve the workspace store, not the packaged one
    
    apps/tasks writers resolve the task store under the process cwd — one task
    store per workspace is the app's contract (store.store_path) — while readers
    went through engine.vertex_* with the packaged vertex file alone, which
    resolves package-relative. A worker wrote its worktree's store and read the
    packaged one: zero tasks. Pre-existing at main; surfaced by sol r3 during the
    jsonl-canonical review, and masked in tests by patching _TASKS_VERTEX.
    
    engine: vertex_read/vertex_facts/vertex_ticks/vertex_summary take an explicit
    `store=` — a canonical locator that answers *where* while the declaration
    still answers *what* (folds, kinds, and via the locator's extension, which
    file is authoritative). Resolved through resolved_index, so a .jsonl override
    materializes and tails its derived index exactly like a declared one. Refused
    on combine/discover: one override cannot select among N member stores.
    
    tasks: lifecycle.workspace_store is the reader half of the split store_path
    documents for writers, threaded from the folds and the fetch_* readers
    (session status/log, task log, project bridge).
    
    tests: the un-masked scenario at both levels — a packaged-style vertex outside
    the workspace, cwd the only thing naming the workspace, no module-state
    patching; .db and .jsonl declarations both. Existing fold tests now chdir into
    their tmp workspace, which is what the contract actually requires.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

